==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Grandmaster Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Masked Grandmaster Cat''' when obtained from [[Infernal Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] of [[Infernal Tower]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Hermit Cat is somewhat like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]], but attacks faster and can fire up to three [[Wave Attack]]s at a time if all his hits connect. Use him to handle certain bosses from a distance by hitting the peons and letting the waves hit the boss. The Wave Attack covers a range of 735, being able to reach even [[Director Kurosawah]]. He also has the valuable niche of being a [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attacker]] usable in {{4c}}, but he faces fierce competition from [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], who is significantly more disposable.

Unfortunately, Hermit's standing range is terrible, meaning you'll have to consider his deployment with care if you want to make the best of his ability.

==='''True Form'''===
Masked Grandmaster Cat gains specialization against [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] through the Strong ability, Curse Immunity and the ability to Curse them. With his DPS and Waves, he can deliver heavy damage to Relics all the while causing a lot of trouble to supporting peons and, possibly, Relic backliners. His Curse will rarely help due to his range and the low activation chance, but he doesn't need it, as his Strong ability and better recharge will make him a threat to several common Relics. Unfortunately, his range still often limits him, as all it takes is for a Relic to have more than 255 range (that isn't [[Loris]]) to render Masked Grandmaster Cat a waste of money. It is therefore better to use him when there are stepping stones such as [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]], burrowing [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], and short-ranged peons. A prime example is [[Soul in the Idol]], where you can abuse the Metal Hippoes to stack Hermits and chip away at [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]] while avoiding his 700-range Omni Strike.

Relics aside, his general performance as a Wave Attacker is also vastly improved in this Form, thanks to his longer Waves, higher health and shorter recharge.

