==Trivia==
*Hermit Cat is a reference to [[wikia:dragonball:Korin|Korin]] from the ''Dragon Ball'' series. Just like Korin, he is a cat who lives on top of a [[Heavenly Tower|Giant Tower]], carries a walking stick, and is deceptively powerful.
**The ''[[wikipedia:Daifuku|mame daifuku]]'' mentioned in Hermit Cat's Japanese description is a sweet rice cake with azuki beans or soybeans mixed into it. This may be another reference to Korin, who is known as the farmer of the legendary [[wikia:dragonball:Senzu Beans|Senzu Beans]], which  have incredible regenerative properties.
**Masked Grandmaster Cat's mask greatly resembles that of [[wikia:dragonball:Grandpa Gohan|Grandpa Gohan]], another character from ''Dragon Ball''.
*Although Hermit Cat is referred to as a "legendary sage" in [[BCEN]], neither of his [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|enemy]] [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|forms]] have the [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] type, as his Japanese descriptions only call him a "hermit" (仙人 ''sennin'') or "old master" (老師 ''rōshi'').
*Masked Grandmaster Cat's design combines both of his previous forms, having the Normal Form's head shape and Evolved Form's beard.
*Grandmaster Cat's head looks fairly similar to one of [[Gamatoto Expedition/Gallery|Gamatoto's costumes]], more specifically, the one you unlock after Gamatoto upgrades to Level 19.

